  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 207 AM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nWe'll maintain a low chance for showers and thunderstorms along the \nseabreeze this afternoon as heat indices once again will flirt with \nHeat Advisory conditions, peaking around 110 over the Coastal \nPlains. Heat will remain our primary concern each afternoon this \nweek, all are urged to continue practicing heat safety.\n\nRain chances increase (20-45%) Wednesday and Thursday as an inverted \nmid-level trough (or low) over the Gulf moves westward into South \nTexas, increasing PWAT values to near 2.25\" (90th percentile) and \nenhancing lift support. Greatest coverage is expected over the \nVictoria Crossroads. A series of weak mid-level disturbances along \nthe southern periphery of the ridge will keep at least low rain \nchances over the Coastal Plains through this upcoming weekend.",
